<title>GERMANY: Sixt says 97 profit forecast &quot;conservative&quot;.</title>
<headline>Sixt says 97 profit forecast &quot;conservative&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car rental firm Sixt AG on Wednesday described its forecast of a rise in 1997 full year profits of between 40 and 50 percent as conservative.</p>
<p>Company chairman Erich Sixt told Reuters the prediction was based on a &quot;conservative estimate&quot;.</p>
<p>He said Sixt did not plan any big purchases with the extra revenue. The company was watching the market carefully but was interested above all in smaller chains or local car hire firms in Europe, Sixt said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom +49 228 26097160</p>
</text>
